It seems to me that a new "Rings" section in the General Techniques
section should be added. I did do a search for ring of conflict and
found it mentioned as an aid for Ludios and the Plane of Air, but it is
certainly useful in other situations. Adding a section specifically for
rings seems to be a good fix for me.

How about a Rings section in three parts?

[1] Extremely helpful rings including free action [late], levitation
[mid & late], conflict [with care early, mid & late], poison resistance
[early], and teleport control [late].

[2] Situational rings including stealth, warning, searching, slow
digestion, see invisible, and the other resistance rings. [many of
these have other methods of getting the intrinsic - point that out too]

[3] "Trap" rings including the ones typically generated cursed (e.g.,
hunger, aggravate monster, teleportation, polymorph).

However, I believe the hard part will be to put the rings into the
three categories (and which ones to ignore). What do you all think?

